l,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["6 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State and bound the cross-env-id timestamp-ordering assumption the overlap rule depends on: note in the Approach that HLC's monotonic floor is per-ticket + a git-ignored per-clone cache (`src/rebar/_store/hlc.py`), so across re-clones ordering is only as strong as physical-clock agreement, and either justify why sub-second skew is tolerable (spans compared at day granularity) or add a skew margin / fall-back so clock skew cannot flip a sequential re-clone into an overlap.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.8,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan step 2: 'A successor's first write must come strictly after its predecessor's last write, so a shared nanosecond timestamp cannot come from succession.'","src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:48-65 `_max_event_prefix` computes the HLC witness floor PER TICKET (ticket_id argument), not store-wide.","src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:92-105 `next_tick` = max(cache, witness, physical_now())+1; the cache (`.rebar/hlc.state`) is a git-ignored per-clone high-water file that a re-clone does NOT carry over (module docstring: 'per-clone high-water cache', ignored).","Consequence: a successor clone's first write to a ticket the predecessor never touched is governed only by `physical_now()`; under wall-clock skew it can be numerically below a predecessor's later write, so per-(env,author) min/max spans can overlap even for a genuinely sequential re-clone."],"finding":"The overlap rule's correctness rests on an unstated assumption that event timestamps are strictly monotonic across env ids, but HLC does not guarantee this across clones for distinct tickets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f35969be172abbdd9","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (and step 3); src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:92-108","norm_id":"n9f2d0bca68bc5d58","priority":0.0,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Two sequential re-clones whose hosts have skewed physical clocks; the successor's early write to a fresh ticket gets a lower HLC than a late predecessor write, so the author's spans overlap and ENV_ID_MISMATCH fires (a false positive — the exact outcome the change aims to remove).","A re-clone that resumes editing the SAME tickets inherits the per-ticket witness floor and is safe, but writes to new tickets are not."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.7,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_